My 4th ascencion, with a conductless barbarian who just wanted to ascend
:)

Not much to mention really, but my barb just waddled through the late
game with no effort whatsoever. 

The game started out with some mindless slaughtering, and a lot of
wallowing around with crappy weapons.

Once I got grayswandir from a wish I finally had a weapon that did
actual damage, since my god kept bringing me all the crappy
stuff. Castle wand was the only wishes I got, though I had a magic lamp
if I needed something in a pinch.

Got a cloak of MR from a bonesfile.

Lategame was increadibly boring :(
With -41 AC and two-weaponing grayswandir and a silver sabre (and barbs
only get BASIC in sabre), he just cut through ANYTHING in no time
whatsoever.

Arch lichs? _3_ turns of attacking, max - never even had to get them at
the upstairs.

Orcus? 2 turns, without him getting off a single shot of his wand.

I can't really remember my two-weaponing valk being this overpowered,
this barb was insane. Genoed ; R, the former out of boredom, the latter
because I didn't bother bringing things to kill them with - whacking
disenchanters with my sabres would be stupid, and I didn't really want
to lug around daggers or wands, which I assume is the normal equipment
for genoless combat characters?

Mind flayers where easy with E-engraving, telepathy let me know they
where coming, so I only got sucked once due to being either confused or
blinded when engraving, not sure.

No nurse-dancing, just a few full healing potions.

I really need to start doing more conduct-games, atleast with the
overpowered classes :)

